<h2>Workflows by Real-World Scenario</h2>
<p>We have organized how modes, agents, and tools are woven together in real situations into eight scenarios. Use the number buttons or the previous/next buttons below to look through the scenarios one at a time.</p>

<div class="carousel">
    <div class="carousel-stage">

        <div class="scn active">
            <h3>Scenario 1 — kicking off a new project</h3>
            <p>When you start an empty project for the first time — proceed in the order documentation → design consensus → requirement clarification → team implementation.</p>
            <pre><code><span class="c"># 1. Document the project structure</span>
/oh-my-claudecode:deepinit
<span class="c"># 2. Architecture consensus (based on expert consensus)</span>
ralplan: design the overall system architecture (Next.js, PostgreSQL, Redis)
<span class="c"># 3. Clarify the core requirements</span>
/deep-interview "a SaaS app with social login"
<span class="c"># 4. Implement the basic features with a team</span>
team ralph: implement all of the basic CRUD features</code></pre>
        </div>

        <div class="scn">
            <h3>Scenario 2 — adding a feature</h3>
            <p>If the requirements are clear, go straight to autopilot; if they are vague, refine them with deep-interview first and then implement.</p>
            <pre><code><span class="c"># When the requirements are clear</span>
autopilot: add email notification features (signup welcome, password reset, order confirmation)
<span class="c"># When the requirements are vague — clarify first</span>
/deep-interview "add a notification feature"
<span class="c"># → implement with the clarified requirements</span>
autopilot: implement with [the clarified requirements]</code></pre>
        </div>

        <div class="scn">
            <h3>Scenario 3 — refactoring legacy code</h3>
            <p>Proceed safely in four steps: grasp the current state → plan → parallel conversion → verification.</p>
            <pre><code><span class="c"># 1. Grasp the current state (technical debt analysis)</span>
deep-analyze: identify the technical debt in this codebase
<span class="c"># 2. Migration plan</span>
/oh-my-claudecode:plan JavaScript → TypeScript migration
<span class="c"># 3. Convert several files in parallel</span>
ulw: convert all 15 of these files to TypeScript
<span class="c"># 4. Verification</span>
review code
fix build</code></pre>
        </div>

        <div class="scn">
            <h3>Scenario 4 — tracking down and fixing a bug</h3>
            <p>If you paste the error message as-is, the debugger analyzes the stack and finds the root cause.</p>
            <pre><code><span class="c"># Paste the error message as-is</span>
deep-analyze:
  Error: Cannot read property 'user' of undefined
  at AuthMiddleware (middleware.ts:45)
<span class="c"># → the debugger analyzes the stack → identifies the root cause → proposes a fix</span>
<span class="c"># Apply the fix</span>
fix build</code></pre>
        </div>

        <div class="scn">
            <h3>Scenario 5 — code review before deployment</h3>
            <p>Run the quality and security reviews in turn, then fix the problems found all at once with ralph.</p>
            <pre><code><span class="c"># 1. Comprehensive code review (logic · anti-patterns · performance)</span>
review code
<span class="c"># 2. Check for security vulnerabilities</span>
security review
<span class="c"># 3. Fix every problem found in one batch</span>
ralph: fix every problem found in the code review</code></pre>
        </div>

        <div class="scn">
            <h3>Scenario 6 — TDD development</h3>
            <p>It automatically repeats the flow of writing tests first and implementing afterwards (Red → Green → Refactor).</p>
            <pre><code><span class="c"># Tests first, implementation later</span>
tdd: develop the user authentication service
<span class="c"># → 1) write test cases  2) failing tests (Red)</span>
<span class="c"># → 3) delegate implementation  4) confirm they pass (Green)  5) refactor</span></code></pre>
        </div>

        <div class="scn">
            <h3>Scenario 7 — data analysis work</h3>
            <p>Several analysis agents run Python (pandas · matplotlib) in parallel to produce a comprehensive report.</p>
            <pre><code><span class="c"># Analyzing log and CSV data</span>
/sciomc analyze this CSV file:
  - user behavior patterns
  - churn cause analysis
  - features with a high contribution to revenue</code></pre>
        </div>

        <div class="scn">
            <h3>Scenario 8 — automating Git work</h3>
            <p>You can delegate commit tidying, writing the PR description, and even branch strategy to git-master.</p>
            <pre><code><span class="c"># Tidy the changed files into commits by meaningful unit</span>
delegate to git-master: tidy the changed files into commits by meaningful unit
<span class="c"># Write the PR description (in Korean, including why · what · tests)</span>
git-master: write the PR description for these changes
<span class="c"># Branch strategy</span>
git-master: work on the feature/auth branch, then prepare a squash merge into main</code></pre>
        </div>

    </div>

